# DMW3 PC Edition stage data v1 (edit in-game with F2 + --dev, or by hand)
# exit  x y w h TARGET [arriveX arriveY]
# npc   talk  SPRITE x y dir "Name" "Line one|Line two"
# walls original = walls from the game's own walk map (DAT/FIELD/STAGE/S###TMPK.BIN)
# npcs original  = also place the original event actors (PRO/WSTAG###.PRO) as NPCs
#
# ASUKA CITY / MAIN LOBBY (S210) - where a new PC Edition game starts (reference shot 38: the player arrives on the
# right platform from the Login Room door, decoded trigger zone 0xA2 at 720,359).
# spawn: in front of that door (the decoded WSTAG spawn 284,308 is the centre emblem used by the opening).
# doors = decoded trigger zones, destinations from the reference playthrough (reference/NOTES.md, shots 37-53):
#   0xA2 (720,359) start-spot door by the teal grid screen -> Asuka City / Login Room       S225 (shot 51)
#   0xA3 (496,263) door right of the Tamer Service counter  -> Asuka City / Arena Front Desk S230 (shots 41, 52-53)
#   0xE1 (704,584) lower-right walkway                       -> Asuka City / Central Sector  S200 (shots 39, 48),
#        arriving at the dragon gate (S200 zone 0xA5, where Tamer Genji waits). Blocked until the player has
#        partners (zones 0x07/0x09, "Oh yeah! I need my partner Digimon data!"): see data/story/chapter1.story.
#   0x20 (56,392) west corridor: destination unknown (not in the reference run); leads to Central Sector for now.
#   0xA4 (320,175) door left of the counter, 0x65 (168,136) upper-left platform: destinations unknown, not linked.
# npcs: the original event actors (WSTAG210); talking shows the ORIGINAL lines from your disc
#   (Tamer Service "hints" counter, Guide "Digimon Online Help Counter", Maniac Phillip, ...).
